## Production‑Ready Environment Variables (what still needs to be set)

| Variable | Purpose | Required in Production? | Example / Guidance |
|----------|---------|--------------------------|--------------------|
| `NODE_ENV` | Sets runtime mode; enables strict checks | **Yes** | `production` |
| `PORT` | Port the API listens on | Optional (defaults to 8080) | `8080` |
| `TRUST_PROXY` | Trust proxy headers (if behind LB/CDN) | Recommended if behind a reverse proxy | `true` |
| `API_KEY` | Protects processing routes; required when `STRICT_PRODUCTION_CONFIG=true` | **Yes** (strong random string) | `3a9fK8z!Bq2$LmNp#Vx7*RtQ` |
| `OUTPUT_SIGNING_SECRET` | Secret for signed download URLs (can reuse API_KEY if ≥16 chars) | **Yes** | `super-secret-signing-key-12345` |
| `CORS_ORIGINS` | Allowed origins for CORS (empty => allow all – not recommended for prod) | **Yes** (restrict) | `https://app.example.com,https://www.example.com` |
| `REDIS_URL` | Connection string for persistent job queue (BullMQ) | **Yes** (unless `RUN_QUEUE_WORKER_IN_API=true` and you accept in‑memory fallback) | `redis://redis:6379` |
| `RUN_QUEUE_WORKER_IN_API` | Whether the API process also runs the job worker | **No** (set `false` in prod and run separate worker) | `false` |
| `ALLOW_IN_MEMORY_QUEUE_FALLBACK` | Fallback to in‑memory queue if Redis unavailable | **No** (set `false` to fail fast) | `false` |
| `STORAGE_PROVIDER` | Where job outputs are stored (`local` or `s3`) | **Yes** (choose `s3` for production durability) | `s3` |
| `S3_BUCKET`, `S3_REGION`, `S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | S3/MinIO credentials (only needed if `STORAGE_PROVIDER=s3`) | **Yes** when using S3 | *Provide your bucket/keys* |
| `MEDIA_URL_INGEST_ENABLED` | Enable/disable URL‑based downloads (YouTube, etc.) | Depends on policy | `true` (if you have reviewed legal implications) |
| `MEDIA_URL_ALLOWLIST` | Restrict URL ingestion to specific domains | Optional but recommended | `youtube.com,vimeo.com` |
| Other media/FFmpeg/OCR/compression vars | Fine‑tune limits, timeouts, engines | Usually fine with defaults; adjust per capacity | See `.env.example` |

*All other variables have sensible defaults and can be left unchanged unless you have specific performance or feature requirements.*

## Remaining Action Items

